# Mental Model — {workspace}

Workspace-scoped cross-repo coupling notes. Architect owns this file and updates it during the tech-design phase. Operator and implementer append entries to the Surprise Log via `/surprise`. Tech-agnostic: do not bake in a language, framework, or runner.

## Domain Glossary

Shared terms across the repos in this workspace. Use this when the same word means different things in different repos, or when a term is non-obvious to a newcomer.

_Empty — populate during tech-design._

## Flag Inventory

Feature flags, env vars, and config keys that affect cross-repo behaviour. Record the key, where it is read, and what it gates.

> Auto-population deferred. Populate by hand during tech-design or via `/surprise` on the first hit.

_Empty — populate during tech-design._

## Coupling Map

Calls (HTTP/RPC), publishes (events/messages), and shares (DB tables, files, schemas) that cross repo boundaries. One row or bullet per edge.

> Auto-population deferred. Populate by hand during tech-design or via `/surprise` on the first hit.

_Empty — populate during tech-design._

## Behavior Conditions

Cross-repo conditional behaviours: "when X is true in repo A, repo B does Y." These are the rules that surprise newcomers and break naive assumptions.

_Empty — populate during tech-design._

## State Diagrams

Mermaid diagrams for cross-repo flows. Optional — only add when a flow is non-obvious from prose.

_Empty — add diagrams here when useful._

## Surprise Log

Append-only log of "the model said X, reality showed Y" moments. Each entry is a dated subsection added by `/surprise`. Do not edit older entries; surprises that are later resolved should be addressed by updating the relevant section above and leaving the log entry intact as history.

